  "id": "tyramine",
  "term": "tyramine",
  "definition": "Tyramine is a naturally occurring substance found in foods such as cheese that indirectly boosts adrenergic signaling rather than directly stimulating adrenergic receptors. It can enter adrenergic uptake pathways, interact with monoamine oxidase, and trigger release of adrenergic transmitters, which can extend their effects.",
